"installation_conditions\": \"same as FMT-Lx\"}\n\nHmm, attributes values — shape? Schema says attributes{} free-form. Rule 2 strict structured values applies to \"characteristic value\". For model attributes, to be safe I could use structured form too: {\"flow_straightener_options\": {\"value\": \"large or small\"}}. Hmm. The R60 example shows models with just model_id, no attributes. Rule: models[]: {model_id, label, attributes{}}. Free-form attributes. I'll use plain strings for attributes — simpler and readable. Actually to be consistent with rule 2's spirit, I could do {\"value\": ..., \"unit_symbol\": null}. But these are descriptive strings, not measured characteristics. I'll keep plain strings. Hmm, risk either way. The schema example in R137 shows models as {\"model_id\": \"G1.6\"} with no attributes. I'll include minimal attributes only where the fragment gives per-model info, as plain string values. That seems reasonable.\n\nActually, let me reconsider whether to include model_family at all. The instruction: \"Return one JSON object conforming to the layered schema for the content present in THIS fragment only.\" The models FMT-L/S/Lx/Dc are present. The config_level references them. Including model_family makes the output self-consistent. I'll include it.\n\nAlso certified_type.module_designation — not applicable/not present. Omit.\n\ndescription for certified_type: Could include the installation-conditions summary? There's a \"description\" field: \"free-text description if present\". The installation conditions text is about installation, not a type description per se. I'll skip, since config_level captures it.\n\nLet me finalize dates format: \"24 December 2014\" → \"2014-12-24\". \"30 July 2015\" → \"2015-07-30\". ISO format is standard for such extraction.\n\nFinal JSON:\n\n{\n  \"certificate\": {\n    \"number\": \"R137/2012-NL1-14.03\",\n    \"project_number\": \"SO15202424\",\n    \"page_total\": 5,\n    \"member_state\": \"The Netherlands\"\n  },\n  \"issuing_authority\": {\n    \"name\": \"NMi\"\n  },\n  \"recommendation\": {\n    \"id\": \"R137\",\n    \"edition\": 2012\n  },\n  \"certified_type\": {\n    \"category\": \"Gas meter\",\n    \"type_designations\": [\"FMT-L\", \"FMT-S\", \"FMT-Lx\", \"FMT-Dc\"]\n  },\n  \"model_family\": {\n    \"family_name\": null,\n    \"models\": [\n      {\"model_id\": \"FMT-L\", \"attributes\": {\"flow_straightener_options\": \"large or small\"}},\n      {\"model_id\": \"FMT-S\", \"attributes\": {\"flow_straightener_options\": \"large only\"}},\n      {\"model_id\": \"FMT-Lx\", \"attributes\": {\"flow_straightener\": \"identical to FMT-S configuration\", \"straight_inlet_requirements\": \"none\"}},\n      {\"model_id\": \"FMT-Dc\", \"attributes\": {\"construction\": \"two FMT-Lx cartridges in one housing\", \"installation_conditions\": \"same as FMT-Lx\"}}\n    ]\n  },\n  \"components\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"flow_straightener\",\n      \"type_designations\": [\"large flow straightener\", \"small flow straightener\"],\n      \"alternatives\": \"OR\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"characteristics\": {\n    \"config_level\": [\n      {\n        \"attribute\": \"minimum_straight_inlet_pipe_length\",\n        \"axis\": \"meter_model_and_flow_straightener\",\n        \"values\": [\n          {\"condition\": \"FMT-L with large flow straightener\", \"value\": 1, \"unit_symbol\": \"DN\"},\n          {\"condition\": \"FMT-L with small flow straightener\", \"value\": 5, \"unit_symbol\": \"DN\"},\n          {\"condition\": \"FMT-S with large flow straightener (only straightener permitted)\", \"value\": 1, \"unit_symbol\": \"DN\"},\n          {\"condition\": \"FMT-Lx, no flow straightener requirement\", \"value\": \"not required\"},\n          {\"condition\": \"FMT-Dc, same conditions as FMT-Lx\", \"value\": \"not required\"}\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"revision_history\": [\n    {\"revision\": \"Initial\", \"date\": \"2014-12-24\"},\n    {\"revision\": \"1\", \"date\": \"2015-